\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{commit}{1c3f2e7}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The arena publishes only its small exports, so \code{\verb~|bench/build-corpus.sh~} builds the complete set with the arena's own build tool at the revision of the published results: 130 test definitions, 270 tests. All 270 exports are byte-identical to the arena's by SHA-256, Mathlib included (6,326,141,213 bytes, 112,081,718 lines). Built side by side on the 20-core development host on 2026-11-23 everything takes about 40 minutes; the slowest is navier-stokes-euler with 32 minutes. The official checker v4.35.0 run over everything except mathlib, cslib and navier-stokes-euler gave 267 of 267 published verdicts; on the three largest corpora it was not run as part of building the corpus.}

\p{Detail: \src{bench/README.md}. Commit \commit{1c3f2e7}. Session: [research, benchmark infrastructure and spikes](ses-XOS5).}
